100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Several real-world systems address traffic signal optimisation using similar approaches. SCOOT \(Split Cycle Offset Optimisation Technique\) is a widely deployed adaptive traffic control system used in cities such as London and Singapore. SCATS \(Sydney Coordinated Adaptive Traffic System\) is another adaptive system used across Australia and internationally. InSync by Rhythm Engineering uses real-time data and machine learning to optimise signal timings dynamically. VISSIM is a microscopic traffic simulation tool used by traffic engineers to test signal timing strategies before deployment.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
